      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release), so this is about twice the limit. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day), which is the max immediate-release dose.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily** (2,000 mg/day), which is a common regimen.\n- **500 mg three times daily** (1,500 mg/day) or another dose.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you meant, please confirm that. I'd suggest you also check it with pharmacy first."
      }
